/node_modules
# dist/ is committed on purpose (not gitignored): this example's whole point
# is that a fresh clone can `go run .` without npm. Rebuild it with
# `npm run build` after touching web/ or ui/ — a stale dist/ is a silent
# staleness bug, not a build error. Do not re-add it here.
*.x.go
.env
# `go build ./...` at the module root writes a binary named after the
# module directory (not caught by *.x.go or /node_modules above).
/streaming-partial
